Session 6, 2026-09-05, Ag Leader InCommand 1200 ALONE on the bus (New
Holland's own VT powered down). Firmware: isobus-tc-client @ 935de81.

THE CLEANEST RESULT OF THE PROJECT SO FAR:
  - VT connects and holds (the #17 fix, confirmed against the very terminal
    that surfaced the bug in Session 5).
  - **The Task Controller connects for the first time ever** -- "DDOP
    Activated without error", tc=Y. Sessions 3, 4 and 5 never got past tc=N.
    This settles #19: it was the same control-function eviction bug, exactly
    as the off-tractor analysis in commit 935de81 predicted, not a TC-GEO
    licensing gate and not a gap in IsobusTcInterface's discovery.
  - Operator confirmed the InCommand 1200 mirrored Ploegbesturing's own
    screen content -- the real working set, not just the app-switcher icon.

Preceded by ~70s of a completely silent bus (busload 0.0%, msgs=0,
vt=N(0/22) with no handshake progress at all) while no terminal was powered
-- a useful negative control: with no VT on the bus, the client sits in
Disconnected and does nothing, exactly as it should.

Timestamps are seconds since the logging script attached to COM4; the board
was rebooted at ~t=543 (banner below), so board-relative time is roughly
t - 547.

